## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical Android patterns: MVVM, Compose bindings, reactive state management, and basic testing. Keeps scope beginner-friendly while still showing discipline in architecture.

## Key Concepts

- MVVM with Jetpack Compose
- StateFlow for UI state
- Basic input validation (email pattern, password length)
- In-memory repository as a stand-in for network calls
- Unit and UI testing strategy

## Code Example

```kotlin
class LoginState(
  val email: String = "",
  val password: String = "",
  val emailError: String? = null,
  val passwordError: String? = null,
  val loading: Boolean = false,
  val loginResult: Boolean? = null
)

class LoginViewModel : ViewModel() {
  private val _state = MutableStateFlow(LoginState())
  val state: StateFlow<LoginState> = _state

  private fun validateEmail(email: String): String? =
    if (android.util.Patterns.EMAIL_ADDRESS.matcher(email).matches()) null else "Invalid email"
  private fun validatePassword(pw: String): String? =
    if (pw.length >= 8) null else "Password too short"

  fun onEmailChange(e: String) {
    _state.value = _state.value.copy(email = e, emailError = validateEmail(e))
  }

  fun onPasswordChange(pw: String) {
    _state.value = _state.value.copy(password = pw, passwordError = validatePassword(pw))
  }

  fun login() {
    val s = _state.value
    val e = s.emailError
    val p = s.passwordError
    if (e != null || p != null) return
    _state.value = s.copy(loading = true)
    viewModelScope.launch {
      val ok = FakeAuthRepository.login(s.email, s.password)
      _state.value = s.copy(loading = false, loginResult = ok)
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to handle network errors and show retry options?
- How would you add automated UI tests for the Compose screen validating error messages and successful login flow?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of core Android app architecture: data layer with Room, network layer with Retrofit, UI with Jetpack Compose, and a practical accessibility feature (TTS). It also touches lifecycle awareness and basic testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Room: entity, DAO, migrations (basic)
- Retrofit: service interfaces and data models
- Kotlin Flow: streaming data from repository to UI
- Jetpack Compose: LazyColumn rendering
- TextToSpeech: initialization, lifecycle handling, easing for UI
- Testing: unit tests for data layer; instrumentation for TTS and UI flows

## Code Example

```kotlin
// Entity
@Entity(tableName = "headlines")
data class Headline(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val title: String,
  val timestamp: Long
)

// DAO
@Dao
interface HeadlineDao {
  @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
  suspend fun insertAll(headlines: List<Headline>)

  @Query("SELECT * FROM headlines ORDER BY timestamp DESC")
  fun getAll(): Flow<List<Headline>>
}
```

```kotlin
// Retrofit service
interface HeadlinesService {
  @GET("headlines")
  suspend fun fetchHeadlines(): List<Headline>
}
```

```kotlin
// Repository sketch
class HeadlinesRepo(private val dao: HeadlineDao, private val svc: HeadlinesService) {
  val headlines: Flow<List<Headline>> = dao.getAll()

  suspend fun refresh() {
    val fresh = svc.fetchHeadlines()
    dao.insertAll(fresh)
  }
}
```

